<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila sets 887 mln pesos for rice, corn project.</title>
<headline>Manila sets 887 mln pesos for rice, corn project.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines has allocated 887.8 million pesos this year to improving the country's rice and corn crops by extending credit to farmers, the Agriculture Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>The department said in a statement it was set to sign an agreement with two state agencies and the Islam Bank to help the government extend credit to farmers' cooperatives.</p>
<p>The scheme is part of the government's rice and corn productivity programme launched last year.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936 Fax 817-6267</p>
